/-!
# Structurality from `Equation4432` through a three-guard companion

Generated by `defwork/itautcell3.py`.  `Equation4432` is `x ◇ (y ◇ x) = (x ◇ x) ◇ x`.  Its guarded obligation
-- a bijection of a finite model commuting with `x □ y = if (M.op a b) = b then (M.op a a) else if a = b then (M.op a a) else if (M.op a a) = (M.op a b) then b else (M.op a b)` is an automorphism of `◇` --
is `GuardAut3_pxy_y_x_y_pxx_pxy_pxx_pxx_y_pxy_Equation4432`, proved elsewhere.  That obligation names no target, so every
law the companion satisfies is another cell for free, and there
are 2 of them below.
-/

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language Law Law.MagmaLaw FreeMagma

set_option maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.unusedTactic false
set_option linter.unreachableTactic false

/-- `Equation3253` from `Equation4432`: `x ◇ (y ◇ x) = (x ◇ x) ◇ x` ⊢ `x ◇ x = x ◇ (x ◇ (x ◇ x))`,
